<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25833" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lăpĭdārĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to stones, stone-</i>
			(ante-class. and post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">latomiae,</span>”
				<i>stone-quarries</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Capt. 3, 5, 65</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">navis,</span>”
				<i>that carries stones</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 117</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lapidariae litterae,</span>”
				<i>cut in stone</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. 58</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">‡OPIFICES,</span>”
				<i>stone-cutters</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4208</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lăpĭdārĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>a
			stonecutter</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 13, 6, 5, § 7</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 4220</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Vulg. Sirach, 45,
			13</span></i>.—*</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Full of stones, stony</i>, for lapidosus: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">campi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 2, 6</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
